  <prompt>
    Retire the BRIEF-NARRATE-CHANNEL catalog Action (via BA editor / Dataverse MCP) and remove its remaining code footprint — the ChannelActionCode constant and any now-dead reference in DailyBriefingNarrator. Achieve grep-zero code consumers of "BRIEF-NARRATE-CHANNEL". Leave BRIEF-NARRATE-TLDR untouched. Per FR-A2 / NFR-05.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Familiar with the ADR-039/040 catalog-Action model, Dataverse Action catalog editing via BA editor/MCP, and the DailyBriefing narrator.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The BRIEF-NARRATE-CHANNEL Action row is retired in the catalog and the ChannelActionCode constant plus any residual code reference is deleted from DailyBriefingNarrator.cs. A repo-wide grep for BRIEF-NARRATE-CHANNEL returns zero hits under src/. BRIEF-NARRATE-TLDR remains present and functional. Eval cases that referenced the channel Action are updated. BFF builds 0 errors; publish size reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 010 removed the per-channel LLM call path, leaving ChannelActionCode unreferenced in the execution path. This task completes the retirement: delete the const, retire the catalog Action data, and prove no code consumer remains. NFR-05 requires grep-zero before merge; the retirement must be coordinated with eval-case updates so the suite stays green.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
